@API = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@REQ = 1

### 1  Login as the tennis coach (a leader)
POST {{API}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach.tennis@example.com",
  "password": "abdellahnsila123#002"
}

### 2  List (expect total 1, user.login = coach_padel, copy its "id" into @REQ above)
###    the "user" object must NOT have email or phone_number
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests

### 3  Page after the last one (expect data [], total still 1)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests?page=2

### 4  Bad page and bad limit (expect 400 for both)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests?page=0

###
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests?limit=51

### 5  Reject (expect { "success": true })
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests/{{REQ}}/reject

### 6  List (expect total 0)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests

### 7  Reject again (expect 409)
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests/{{REQ}}/reject

### 8  Request that does not exist (expect 404)
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests/99999/reject

### 9  Id is text (expect 400)
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests/abc/reject

### 10  Login as nsila (a plain member)
POST {{API}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user7@gmail.com",
  "password": "abdellahnsila123#002"
}

### 11  A plain member lists (expect 403)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests

### 12  A plain member rejects (expect 403)
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests/{{REQ}}/reject

### 13  Login as the padel coach, back in the queue
POST {{API}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coach.padel@example.com",
  "password": "abdellahnsila123#002"
}

### 14  Status after the rejection (expect has_pending_request false)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/status

### 15  Not a member of tennis, lists (expect 403)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join-requests

### 16  Ask again (expect pending, the SAME row is reopened) and leave it pending for step 5
POST {{API}}/clubs/tennis/join

### 17  Status (expect has_pending_request true)
GET {{API}}/clubs/tennis/status